---
layout: base.njk
bare: true
---
{#
  Links layout: a "link in bio" page (src/links.md) -- one narrow column
  of large tap targets, meant to be opened from a social profile on a phone.
  Chains to base.njk with `bare: true`, which drops the site header, nav
  and footer so the links are the only thing on the page.

  There is no parsing here. The Markdown is ordinary headings and bullet
  lists; style.css (.links) turns every list item into a card whose whole
  area is the link. So anything Markdown can express works, and the page
  is still a plain, readable list of links with CSS switched off.

  Optional frontmatter:
    image / imageAlt  round avatar above the name (also the OG image)
-#}
<article class="links">
  {% if image -%}
  <img class="links-avatar" src="{{ image | url }}" alt="{{ imageAlt or title }}" width="96" height="96">
  {%- endif %}
  <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
  {{ content | safe }}
  <p class="links-home"><a href="{{ '/' | url }}">{{ site.url | replace("https://", "") }}</a></p>
</article>
